REWRITE details.tsx redirect properly. Move the useEffect ABOVE the early return AND guard against post-success re-renders using a ref. Suggested patch:

  const router = useRouter();
  const draft = useDraft((s) => s.draft);
  const patchDraft = useDraft((s) => s.patchDraft);
  const hadDraftRef = useRef(false);
  useEffect(() => { if (draft) hadDraftRef.current = true; }, [draft]);
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!draft && !hadDraftRef.current) router.replace('/transfer/new');
  }, [draft, router]);
  if (!draft) return null;

This ensures the redirect only fires on a truly empty mount (deep-link / refresh), not when the draft is cleared post-success while the screen is still mounted underneath.
